{
  "id": "church",
  "kind": "api",
  "title": "Breeze ChMS (gracechurch)",
  "description": "Breeze ChMS church database at gracechurch.breezechms.com: Pastoral care and giving reports",
  "credential": {
    "label": "Breeze API key",
    "description": "The church's API key from Breeze → Extensions → API (https://gracechurch.breezechms.com/extensions/api). It has no scopes: it reaches the whole account, giving included. The connector sends it only to gracechurch.breezechms.com.",
    "placeholder": "Paste Breeze API key"
  },
  "guide": {
    "summary": "Sensitive church data, fieldId decoding, two id kinds, undocumented giving reads, and endpoint-split hatches.",
    "content": "# Breeze ChMS usage\n\nChurch database for gracechurch.breezechms.com (Breeze ChMS, now Tithely Church Management): people, tags, events, attendance, forms, volunteers, and giving.\n\nChurch purpose: Pastoral care and giving reports\n\n## Sensitive data: reduce in code\n\nPeople records carry home addresses, phones, birthdates, and family ties, and\ngiving records reveal who gives and how much — religious affiliation by proxy.\nRead them inside `execute_code` and return only the counts, totals, or the\nfew fields the task needs. Never echo whole profiles or donor lists.\n\n## Ids and profile fields\n\n- Ids are numeric strings. Read them from a list tool; never guess one.\n- Events have two ids: an instance id (`list_events` `id`) for one\n  occurrence, and a series `eventId`. Attendance, volunteers, and\n  check-in take the instance id.\n- Person `details` are keyed by profile `fieldId`, not by name. Call\n  `list_profile_fields` once and map ids to names in code. Multiple-choice\n  values and `list_people` filters use option ids from the same call;\n  join several with `-`.\n- `list_people` has no name search. List without details and match names\n  in code, then `get_person` the hits.\n- Projections rename Breeze's snake_case fields to camelCase and drop photo\n  paths and internal columns; `raw: true` returns Breeze's rows.\n\n## Pagination\n\n`list_people` pages by `cursor`: continue while `page.hasMore`. Breeze\nreports no total, so a full page sets `hasMore` and the next may be empty.\n`list_events` and `list_account_log` do not page: `truncated: true`\nmeans narrow the date range. Other lists return everything.\n\n## Giving\n\n`list_contributions` and `list_funds` call endpoints Breeze removed from\nits public reference in 2023 but still serves. They may change or vanish\nwithout notice; a failure there is not your argument's fault. Amounts are\ndecimal strings; `totalAmount` is an exact sum. Online gifts processed by\nTithe.ly arrive through its sync, batched per deposit, so the latest days\nmay be missing. Read the currency from `get_account_summary`.\n\n## Writes and the hatches\n\n- Every write, `add_person`, `assign_tag`, and `record_check_in`\n  included, follows the routing in the `usage` skill. Fetch it with\n  `skills({ name: \"usage\" })` for guest API and write rules.\n  Those three only add, and `add_person` never deduplicates.\n- `update_person` field values: text, date (M/D/YYYY), or option id in\n  `response`; email, phone, address, and family_role values in `details`.\n- Every Breeze call is a GET, writes included, so the hatches split by\n  endpoint. `breeze_api_get` admits only reviewed read endpoints and their\n  documented parameters, such as `/tags/list_folders`,\n  `/events/list_event`, `/events/attendance/eligible`, `/giving/view`,\n  and `/pledges/list_campaigns`; it refuses anything else. Everything else\n  — event, family, volunteer, and form writes, giving writes, check-out,\n  undocumented parameters — is `breeze_api_mutate`. Paths are below\n  `/api`; `*_json` values may be passed as objects.\n- `list_account_log` actions include person_created, person_updated,\n  person_deleted, tag_assign, tag_unassign, event_created,\n  attendance_deleted, form_entry_updated, contribution_added,\n  contribution_updated, contribution_deleted, and batch_updated.\n\n## Rate limits\n\nBreeze publishes no limit and sends no rate headers; a third party reports\nabout 20 requests per minute. Keep loops sequential and prefer one list call\nover many single reads.\n"
  },
  "tools": [
    {
      "name": "breeze_api_get",
      "description": "Call a reviewed Breeze read endpoint and return its response as sent, less calendar feed addresses. Refuses every path and parameter not on the read allowlist, since Breeze writes are GETs too.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "path": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 2,
            "maxLength": 100,
            "description": "Path below /api, e.g. /tags/list_folders. No query string."
          },
          "query": {
            "type": "array",
            "maxItems": 30,
            "description": "Query parameters as name/value pairs.",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "name": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "minLength": 1,
                  "maxLength": 64,
                  "description": "Parameter name, e.g. fields_json."
                },
                "value": {
                  "type": [
                    "string",
                    "number",
                    "boolean",
                    "object",
                    "array"
                  ],
                  "description": "Value; objects and arrays are JSON-encoded for *_json parameters."
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "name",
                "value"
              ],
              "additionalProperties": false
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "path"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "outputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "result": {
            "description": "Breeze's response, less calendar feed addresses and embed keys."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "result"
        ]
      },
      "annotations": {
        "readOnlyHint": true
      }
    },
